    "sha": "936f1c2229eff83518ca49208282d6f270ed2560",
    "commit": {
      "committer": {
        "date": "2026-08-30T13:48:01Z"
      },
      "message": "Install Vercel Web Analytics\n\n# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report\n\n## Summary\nSuccessfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Express.js project following the latest official documentation from Vercel.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Package Installation\n- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/analytics` version `^2.0.1`\n- **Modified files**: \n  - `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics to dependencies\n  - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency lockfile entries\n\n### 2. Existing Configuration Verified\nThe project already had Vercel Analytics properly configured in the HTML templates. The implementation includes:\n\n- **Web Analytics**: Script at `/_vercel/insights/script.js` with proper initialization\n- **Speed Insights**: Script at `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` with proper initialization\n- **Location**: `views/partials/head.ejs`\n\nBoth scripts are:\n- Properly deferred for optimal page load performance\n- Initialized with the correct window objects (`window.va` and `window.si`)\n- Using Vercel's standard endpoints\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nFor Express.js applications using EJS templates (or any server-side rendered HTML), the recommended approach is to include the Vercel Analytics scripts directly in the HTML, which is exactly what this project does.\n\nThe analytics scripts are included in the `<head>` section of `views/partials/head.ejs`:\n\n```html\n<script>\n  window.va = window.va || function () { (window.va.q = window.va.q || []).push(arguments); };\n</script>\n<script defer src=\"/_vercel/insights/script.js\"></script>\n\n<script>\n  window.si = window.si || function () { (window.siq = window.siq || []).push(arguments); };\n</script>\n<script defer src=\"/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js\"></script>\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n✅ Package successfully installed\n✅ Server starts without errors\n✅ Analytics scripts are correctly rendered in HTML output\n✅ No breaking changes introduced\n✅ Build completes successfully\n\n## Next Steps\n\nTo enable analytics in the Vercel dashboard:\n1. Navigate to your project in the Vercel dashboard\n2. Select \"Analytics\" in the sidebar\n3. Click the \"Enable\" button\n4. Deploy the application to Vercel\n5. Analytics data will start flowing after users visit the site\n\n## Notes\n\n- The `@vercel/analytics` package is installed as requested and is available for future use if the project needs programmatic access to analytics features\n- The current implementation using script tags is the correct approach for Express.js/EJS applications according to Vercel documentation\n- Analytics only track in production mode (not in development)\n- The implementation is privacy-friendly and complies with Vercel's privacy standards\n\nCo-authored-by: Vercel <vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>"
    }
  },
